From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lauri Nomme <lauri.nomme@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 20 Sep 2026 18:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_eth_soc: run RX NAPI in softirq context (A/B)

The shared tx/rx NAPI set rides on the dummy netdevice with threaded = 1,
so RX is serviced by napi/mtk_eth-* kthreads (per-packet wake/schedule
overhead on this path). Upstream mainline and frank-w run NAPI in softirq
context. This A/B test flips threaded = 0 to quantify the kthread overhead
on the MT7988 ingress path at MTU 1500; revert once measured.

Signed-off-by: Lauri Nomme <lauri.nomme@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
@@ -6409,7 +6409,7 @@ static int mtk_probe(struct platform_dev
 		dev_err(eth->dev, "failed to allocated dummy device\n");
 		goto err_deinit_ppe;
 	}
-	eth->dummy_dev->threaded = 1;
+	eth->dummy_dev->threaded = 0;
 	strcpy(eth->dummy_dev->name, "mtk_eth");
 	netif_napi_add(eth->dummy_dev, &eth->tx_napi, mtk_napi_tx);
 	netif_napi_add(eth->dummy_dev, &eth->rx_napi[0].napi, mtk_napi_rx);
